type: domain
namespace: SEC
version: "6.0.0"
anchor_version: ">=6.0.0"
maintainer: "Anchor Core"
opt_in: true
source: "U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) Regulatory Framework"

rules:
  - id: "SEC-REG-SCI"
    name: "SEC Regulation SCI — System Capacity & Loop Circuit Breaker"
    original_id: "17 CFR § 242.1001"
    maps_to: "OPS-001"
    obligation_type: detection
    statutes: "SEC Regulation SCI (Systems Compliance and Integrity)"
    severity: "blocker"
    min_severity: "blocker"
    description: >
      Your code contains an unbounded execution loop or unthrottled API call stream within a high-frequency trading pipeline.
      Under structural stress, these uncontrolled iterations risk causing host cluster capacity failure or exchange rate spam,
      directly violating SEC Regulation SCI mandates.

  - id: "SEC-RULE-15C3"
    name: "SEC Rule 15c3-5 — Pre-Trade Financial Limit & Credit Control"
    original_id: "17 CFR § 240.15c3-5"
    maps_to: "LEG-001"
    obligation_type: detection
    statutes: "SEC Exchange Act Rule 15c3-5 (Market Access Rule)"
    severity: "blocker"
    min_severity: "blocker"
    description: >
      An active order routing or trading function is executing without pre-trade credit verification parameters.
      The SEC Market Access Rule strictly mandates that automated market orders pass through pre-trade financial limits
      and capital verification checks before exiting the network layer.

  - id: "SEC-PDA-CONFLICT"
    name: "SEC Predictive Analytics Rule — Fiduciary Conflict & Deceptive Nudges"
    original_id: "SEC Release IA-6353"
    maps_to: "ETH-001"
    obligation_type: detection
    statutes: "SEC Predictive Analytics Conflict of Interest Rule"
    severity: "blocker"
    min_severity: "error"
    description: >
      The agent's optimization prompt or behavioral template is configured to maximize broker commissions or firm revenue over investor interest.
      Proposed SEC guidelines explicitly prohibit deployment of manipulative behavioral nudges that conflict with primary fiduciary duties.

  - id: "SEC-RULE-206"
    name: "SEC Rule 206(4)-1 — Market Manipulation & Rumor Execution Gate"
    original_id: "IA Act Rule 206(4)-1"
    maps_to: "ETH-002"
    obligation_type: detection
    statutes: "Investment Advisers Act Rule 206(4)-1"
    severity: "blocker"
    min_severity: "blocker"
    description: >
      Your trading execution script is configured to trigger financial order volumes based entirely on unverified social web scraping.
      This creates severe corporate vulnerability to artificial market rumor manipulation, violating Anti-Fraud Rule 206(4)-1.

  - id: "SEC-FORM-8K"
    name: "SEC Form 8-K / Reg S-P — Cyber Incident Secret & Exfiltration Gate"
    original_id: "Item 1.05 Form 8-K"
    maps_to: "SEC-002"
    obligation_type: detection
    statutes: "SEC 2024 Cybersecurity Risk & Incident Disclosure"
    severity: "blocker"
    min_severity: "blocker"
    description: >
      An outbound network payload or logging telemetry stream is attempting to export critical environment secrets or topology maps.
      Exposing access infrastructure parameters leaks sensitive firm boundaries, triggering mandatory SEC Form 8-K disclosure vulnerabilities.

  - id: "SEC-FINRA-3110"
    name: "FINRA Rule 3110/4511 — Tamper-Evident 6-Year Log Retention"
    original_id: "FINRA Rule 4511"
    maps_to: "DAC-AuditEntry"
    obligation_type: provenance
    statutes: "FINRA Supervision & Books/Records Rules"
    severity: "blocker"
    min_severity: "blocker"
    description: >
      The local transaction logging protocol does not attach an immutable, Ed25519-signed verification signature block to model inputs.
      FINRA rules mandate tamper-evident ledger preservation for all algorithmic prompts and trading decisions for post-hoc regulatory inspection.
